469 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 964 0 R
/E (What is a Kubernetes NetworkPolicy?)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
470 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 965 0 R
/E (A NetworkPolicy is a Kubernetes resource that controls the traffic flow at the IP address or port level between pods and/or namespaces. It uses labels to define rules that allow or deny ingress and egress traffic.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
471 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 966 0 R
/E (What are the types of traffic a NetworkPolicy can control?)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
