/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 968 0 R
/E (Egress: Traffic going out from a pod.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
474 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 969 0 R
/E (Does Kubernetes apply any default network policies?)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
475 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 970 0 R
/E (No, by default Kubernetes allows all traffic between pods. Only when a NetworkPolicy is applied does Kubernetes start restricting traffic.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
476 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 971 0 R
/E (What is the default behavior when multiple NetworkPolicies apply to a pod?)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
477 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 972 0 R
/E ( They are additive. If multiple policies apply to a pod, the union of the rules is applied traffic is allowed if any policy allows it.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
